  <body>
    <sec id="s1" sec-type="intro">
      <title>1. Introduction</title>
      <p>Patients on <bold>maintenance hemodialysis</bold> lose about 10&#8211;12 g of amino acids per session<sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B4">4</xref></sup>. Values such as 5.5&#160;mmol/L, 10<sup>9</sup>/L and 25&#160;&#181;mol/L must stay exact, as must H<sub>2</sub>O and <italic>P</italic> &lt; 0.05 [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B5">5</xref>&#8211;<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B7">7</xref>]. See <xref ref-type="table" rid="T1">Table 1</xref> and the site <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://example.org/renal">renal guide</ext-link>.</p>
      <p>Second paragraph with a * asterisk and an_underscore.</p>
    </sec>
    <sec id="s2">
      <title>2. Methods</title>
      <sec id="s2a">
        <title>2.1 Search strategy</title>
        <p>We searched three databases. The criteria were:</p>
        <list list-type="bullet">
          <list-item><p>adults aged &#8805;18 years;</p></list-item>
          <list-item><p>on dialysis for &gt;3 months, including:</p>
            <list list-type="order">
              <list-item><p>hemodialysis;</p></list-item>
              <list-item><p>hemodiafiltration.</p></list-item>
            </list>
          </list-item>
        </list>
      </sec>
      <sec id="s2b">
        <title>2.2 Statistical analysis</title>
        <p>The estimated effect was
          <disp-formula id="e1"><alternatives><mml:math><mml:mi>x</mml:mi><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:math><tex-math>x = 1</tex-math></alternatives></disp-formula>
          in all analyses.</p>
      </sec>
    </sec>
    <sec id="s3">
      <title>3. Results</title>
      <p>Daily targets are summarised below.
        <table-wrap id="T1" position="float">
          <label>Table 1.</label>
          <caption><title>Daily nutrient targets by dialysis modality</title><p>Values are per kg of ideal body weight.</p></caption>
          <table frame="hsides" rules="groups">
            <thead>
              <tr><th rowspan="2">Nutrient</th><th colspan="2" align="center">Modality</th></tr>
              <tr><th>HD</th><th>PD</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Protein (g/kg/day)</td><td>1.0&#8211;1.2</td><td>1.0&#8211;1.2<sup>a</sup></td></tr>
              <tr><td rowspan="2">Energy</td><td>25&#8211;35 kcal/kg</td><td>25&#8211;35 kcal/kg</td></tr>
              <tr><td colspan="2">Individualise to activity level</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Sodium | salt</td><td>&lt;2 g/day</td><td>&lt;2 g/day</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn1"><label>a</label><p>Includes protein lost in dialysate.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot>
        </table-wrap>
        The table above is complete.</p>
      <fig id="F1" fig-type="figure">
        <label>Figure 1</label>
        <caption><title>Flow of studies through the review.</title></caption>
        <graphic xlink:href="f1.jpg"/>
      </fig>
      <boxed-text id="bx1"><caption><title>Key points</title></caption><p>Monitor serum potassium monthly.</p></boxed-text>
    </sec>
